# Acknowledgement list for checkpoint ancestry in redblue `main`.
#
# Audited by `tests/checkpoint_ancestry_test.rs`. Parsed, not skimmed: an
# entry without a `|`-separated reason is rejected, so a SHA cannot be
# recorded without saying why it is tolerated.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
# `rbops/dispatch.sh` resumes an interrupted phase with a real `git merge`, so
# a phase checkpointed mid-flight reached `main` without passing the reviewer.
# The commits below are those checkpoints. All of them carry code that no human
# reviewed.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* DONE
# Published history is not rewritten. No rebase, no filter-branch, no reset, no
# amend of an already-published commit. No force-push is attempted by this file,
# by the audit, or by any gate - AGENTS.md §1.6 forbids it. Erasing these
# commits would make the audit green by destroying the evidence, which is the
# opposite of what it is for.
#
# WHAT TO DO IF A NEW ONE APPEARS
# A new line here means somebody has looked at what the commit introduced and
# decided it can stay. A new commit WITHOUT a line here fails the audit.

# --- rbops: phase-NNN checkpoint commits in main's ancestry -----------------
#
# Each reached main through `Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/rbops-wip/...'`
# (see wip_merges_on_main below). dispatch.sh now resumes with
