commit 83d36a7f3d578047d13658d5de4487b7ec1efae7
Author: authorss81 <authorss81@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 6 07:24:10 2026 +0530

    rbops: generate a prompt for every phase the auditor creates
    
    The first audit ran and appended 11 evidence-backed phases to phases.json -
    24 to 35, all citing real src/ files: break/skip not leaving the loop, the
    comparison symbols never being lexed, `unless` unimplemented, reachable panics
    in the time builtins. The self-improving loop works.
    
    None of the 11 had a phases/<id>/PROMPT.md. cmd_run dies on a missing prompt:
    
        [ -f "$prompt" ] || die "no PROMPT.md for $phase - an undeclared prompt is not a phase"
    
    so all 11 were queue entries that would kill their own run, and validate failed
    with 11 missing-prompt errors. Fixed by running gen-prompts.sh, but the contract
    that produced the gap is what needed fixing.
    
    Three changes, because the gap was in three places:
    
    The auditor contract now has a Step 5 that generates a prompt per phase, tells
    it to use gen-prompts.sh rather than hand-writing, and requires a verification
    loop over every id in the manifest that must print nothing. validate already
    caught this - it went to 9/11 - but as a report, not as a rule.
    
    gen-prompts.sh now renders `must_touch` and `failure_assert` into the brief. The
    manifest carried must_touch on 14 phases and the prompts said nothing about it,
    so an agent reading only its own brief could not know it had to change src/ at
    all - which is the entire point of the rule. An exempt phase now states that the
    failure-assertion rule does not apply to it and why, instead of leaving the
    agent to invent a failure test that cannot exist for a linter.
    
    Smoke section 25 enforces manifest/prompt parity in both directions: every
    phase directory has a prompt, no directory is missing from the manifest, every
    must_touch phase states it, and every exempt phase explains the exemption.
    
    117 smoke checks, 11/11 validate, gate 33/33.

